---
import { SITE } from "@/data/site"
---

<article
  class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 md:flex-row"
>
  <div
    class="[&>p]:mb-4 [&>p>strong]:text-yellow-500 dark:[&>p>strong]:text-yellow-100 [&>p>strong]:font-normal [&>p>strong]:font-mono text-pretty order-2 md:order-1"
  >
    <p>
      I'm Dylan, an Integration Engineer at {SITE.company}. I spend my days <strong>designing, building and supporting enterprise APIs</strong> — REST and SOAP services, microservices and the glue that lets business systems talk to each other reliably.
    </p>

    <p>
      I started in <strong>networking and IT support</strong> (CCNA, Cybersecurity Essentials), troubleshooting production incidents with Wireshark and tcpdump. That background shapes how I build today: <strong>security first</strong>, with shared OAuth/JWT and encryption services that standardize API access across multiple applications.
    </p>

    <p>
      Lately I've been connecting <strong>AI agents to enterprise platforms</strong>: MCP servers for SoftExpert SE Suite, the Microsoft Teams integration for IsaStudio and RAG services with FastAPI and pgvector. I'm studying Systems Engineering at UPI and I care about automation, reliable platforms and continuous improvement.
    </p>
  </div>

  <img
    width="256"
    height="256"
    src={SITE.avatar}
    alt={`Photo of ${SITE.name}`}
    loading="lazy"
    class="order-1 object-cover w-64 h-full p-1 md:order-2 rotate-3 lg:p-2 lg:w-64 aspect-square rounded-2xl bg-black/20 dark:bg-yellow-500/5 ring-1 ring-black/70 dark:ring-white/20"
    style="object-position: 50% 50%"
  />
</article>
